// The crate root the PREFLIGHT and SETUP gates built — kept as the record of what they proved.
//
// Both gates run before the deliverable's crate root can exist: preflight before the program has
// even been analyzed, and setup being the step that authors the fixture that root is built around.
// So they build a root of their own, under the same `[[bin]]` NAME as the deliverable (the crucible
// CLI only ever executes `target/<profile>/invariant_test`) at a different path. That is what lets
// `src/main.rs` be written exactly once per run, and never exist as a half-finished crate.
//
// In the delivered crate this file is NOT a build target — `Cargo.toml` points `[[bin]]` at
// `src/main.rs`. The probe itself is still live there, as a section like any other:
//
//     crucible run {{ program }} {{ probe_feature }} --release --dry-run
//
{{ root }}
